WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.200
Really?

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.500
There's benefits to being second place?

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.870
I mean, didn't Ricky Bobby's father say second
place is the first loser?

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:14.580
Even I think Vince Lombardi once said winning
isn't everything, it's the only thing.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.580
Right.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:21.721
So, Patrick, how can you do a Valuetainment
episode titled The Benefits of Being Second

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:22.721
Place, right?

00:00:22.721 --> 00:00:26.310
And you'll understand what I'm talking about
here as I get into my message because I think

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:30.460
it's very important for you to realize that
before Apple became first place, they were

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:33.860
last or second place for a long time.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:39.060
Before anybody becomes first place, they're
not first for a very long time, and this is

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.470
a very important strategy for you to be paying
attention to today as an entrepreneur as you're

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:46.000
building your business because there's a lot
of power behind it.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.130
So the way I want to explain to you the power
of this is by giving you a story.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:55.050
In the rental car business, there are two
companies that we've all heard about.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.440
One you have Hertz, and you have Avis.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.590
These guys rent cars for a living.

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:02.460
That's how they make their living, by renting
cars.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:06.610
Many, many years ago, Avis kept trying to
beat Hertz.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.049
So here's what they did.

00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:10.710
They kept trying to say, "We're going to be
first place.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:11.880
We're going to be first place.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:13.079
We're going to be first place.

00:01:13.079 --> 00:01:14.219
We're better than Hertz.

00:01:14.219 --> 00:01:15.219
We're better than Hertz.

00:01:15.219 --> 00:01:16.219
We're better than Hertz."

00:01:16.219 --> 00:01:17.219
It didn't work.

00:01:17.219 --> 00:01:20.090
They tried this campaign for 13 straight years.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:22.829
And you know what happened for 13 straight
years for Avis?

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:23.890
They lost money.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.030
Not even zero.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:28.429
They lost money 13 straight years.

00:01:28.429 --> 00:01:30.229
Avis lost money.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:31.679
Hertz kept making money.

00:01:31.679 --> 00:01:32.930
They [Avis] kept losing money.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:35.499
Finally the marketing team came together and
said, "Listen guys.

00:01:35.499 --> 00:01:37.390
This is not working out.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.979
We are not first place.

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:43.109
Let's stop trying to do this and let's change
our entire marketing plan."

00:01:43.109 --> 00:01:44.389
And they said, "What do you have in mind?"

00:01:44.389 --> 00:01:46.240
Well, here's what we need to do.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.240
Are we first place?

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.450
No, Hertz is first place.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.560
We're second place.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.560
Yes.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.560
Why don't we say that?

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.799
What do you mean why don't we say that?

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:55.719
Why don't we tell the customer we're second
place?

00:01:55.719 --> 00:01:58.299
And because we're second place, this matters
to us.

00:01:58.299 --> 00:01:59.729
You matter to us.

00:01:59.729 --> 00:02:01.189
Has this guy lost his mind?

00:02:01.189 --> 00:02:03.179
No, we need to do that!

00:02:03.179 --> 00:02:05.200
Because there's two different types of customers.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.159
What are the different types of customers?

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:13.370
You have customers that love underdog companies,
and they always want to buy from underdog

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:14.370
companies.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:17.160
And you have customers that always want to
buy from the best.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.739
I only buy the best!

00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:20.390
I only buy the best!

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.520
And you know what's the difference between
these two types of customers?

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:23.520
You ready for this?

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:24.520
Here's the difference.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.819
The #1 customers are bandwagon customers.

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:30.620
You know how these fans always change the
best, favorite team they have because it's

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.310
a new team that's wining now, so now they're
the bandwagon fans.

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.890
The moment that team starts losing, now there's
this fan.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.430
Oh, I'm a Miami Heat fan.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.680
No, no, I'm a Cleveland Cavaliers fan.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.700
I don't care what fan I am, as long as someone's
winning, I'm a fan of the number one.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:45.700
Right?

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.700
But then you have the loyal fans.

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:47.969
Chicago Cubs, loyal fans.

00:02:47.969 --> 00:02:49.930
Red Sox, loyal fans.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.650
there are loyal fans.

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:56.140
These are loyal fans that stick around and
say, "Listen, I've been a Cubs fan for 29

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:57.140
years.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.959
I'm just a loyal fan, because I'm loyal to
them.

00:03:00.959 --> 00:03:04.450
Because there's a certain emotional connection
to an underdog company.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.060
There's a certain emotional connection to
an underdog organization or sports team.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.469
I'm connected to him.

00:03:09.469 --> 00:03:11.460
I'm not emotionally connected here [number
1].

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.760
I just want to know they're the best.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.470
And this changes all the time.

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.510
Because no one stays number one forever.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.079
But underdog is forever.

00:03:19.079 --> 00:03:20.870
This lasts a lifetime.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.180
Okay?

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:27.790
So Avis vs. Hertz, finally this guy convinces
everybody in the company that our marketing

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.010
campaign moving forward is the following.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:34.440
"Avis is only second in rental cars.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.579
So why go with us?

00:03:37.579 --> 00:03:39.349
We try harder."

00:03:39.349 --> 00:03:41.150
Because we try harder.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:42.390
Because we try harder.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.580
Meaning, we can't afford to lose you.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.580
Hertz can lose you.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:46.580
You're just another customer.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.580
They have so many of them.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:48.871
But we can't afford to lose you.

00:03:48.871 --> 00:03:50.239
You mean a lot to us."

00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:53.189
The moment they change their marketing plan
to this, you know what happened?

00:03:53.189 --> 00:03:59.879
The next year they made $1.2 million in profits,
then $2.6 million of profits, then $5 million

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:00.879
of profits.

00:04:00.879 --> 00:04:01.879
Then you know what happened?

00:04:01.879 --> 00:04:05.049
A new regime came and they went back to what?

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:06.489
"We're going to be number one!"

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:08.569
and then they started losing again.

00:04:08.569 --> 00:04:12.840
If they would have stuck to this game plan,
they would have eventually passed them up.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.969
But because they adjusted too soon, they didn't
pass them up.

00:04:15.969 --> 00:04:19.630
So it's important for you to realize as you're
building your business, if you're sitting

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:24.220
with somebody, and your client asks you the
following thing.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:28.050
Your client asks you a question and they say,
"Well, you know what's the difference between

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.830
you and xyz company?

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.440
They say they're number one."

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.440
Right?

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:33.440
You ready what you're going to say?

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.810
Here's what you're going to say.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:38.440
Mr. Jones, ma'am, you are right.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.760
They are number one.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.430
But this is why you matter to us more.

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.680
They can afford to lose you.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.310
See, I can't afford to lose you.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.700
I have to do my best to make sure I earn your
loyalty.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:53.360
And that means a lot to me, and I hope that
means a lot to you, as much as it means to

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:54.360
me.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.220
Because I want to do whatever I can to make
sure you are serviced properly, at the highest

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.380
possible level.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:02.070
So if that's important to you, I would highly
recommend you do business with me.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.170
Does that make any sense?

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:04.170
Yes it does.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.170
Can we move forward?

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.230
No problem.

00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:10.360
Take that approach, and do not be afraid to
sit with people that are gorillas.

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:13.200
I'm in an industry myself, where we are not
number one.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.500
There's a lot of guys bigger than us, but
we are doing our part.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.510
We are doing our part, and quietly we've been
growing.

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:23.930
And as we sit with these other guys and we're
doing our part, we have done our best to treat

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:29.330
our agents better than anybody else, our customers,
our executives, our staff, our partners, because

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.900
it matters to us.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.410
It matters to us!

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.801
While the guys at the top want to bully, we're
coming up, is what we're doing.

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:38.400
And we're doing our best to take care of everybody
more.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.840
Take that approach as an entrepreneur while
you're doing your business and you'll be amazed

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:45.871
how much more customers will love the fact
that you're being transparent with them, and

00:05:45.871 --> 00:05:48.320
how much more are they going to appreciate
the fact that you're going above and beyond

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:53.180
everybody else to make sure you service those
customers, the employees, the clients, the

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:56.360
partners, the vendors that I've chosen to
do business with.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:01.650
So with that being said, the message is, there
are a lot of benefits to being second place.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:02.750
This is definitely one of them.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:05.882
By the way, if you eventually end up being
first place, you've got to kind of adjust

00:06:05.882 --> 00:06:08.180
your marketing strategy, just so you know
that.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:10.530
Because this doesn't work once you become
first place.

00:06:10.530 --> 00:06:15.861
Then you've got to have a whole different
play that you got to have in order for you

00:06:15.861 --> 00:06:16.861
to get up there.

